---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageMasthead from "../components/PageMasthead.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Racquet Habit"
  description="Read how Racquet Habit collects, uses, stores and shares personal information when you browse the site or place an order."
>
  <PageMasthead
    title="Privacy policy"
    intro="This notice explains the limited information used by racquethabit.com and how our checkout, email and measurement providers handle it."
    issue="Site policy · Effective 31 July 2026"
  />

  <article class="policy-page">
    <aside><span>Plain-language notice</span><span>Last updated 31 July 2026</span><span>Applies to racquethabit.com</span></aside>
    <div>
      <section><h2>1. Who this notice covers</h2><p>This policy covers the Racquet Habit website at racquethabit.com. Current product checkout, payment, fulfillment and order support are provided by Fourthwall under its own privacy terms. When you leave this site for Fourthwall, its notice applies to the information you provide there.</p></section>
      <section><h2>2. Information this site uses</h2><p>The site stores your shopping bag and privacy choices in your browser’s local storage. Essential storage stays on your device until you clear it. Microsoft Clarity runs on every visit and may process page content and rendering, navigation, clicks, pointer movements, scrolling, device and browser details, approximate location, referral source, timestamps and technical errors to reconstruct how the site was used. Form fields and the Court Notes form are masked before Clarity receives them. Without analytics storage, Clarity operates without cookies and does not persist a visitor identity across pages. Where analytics storage is active, Google Analytics may process pages viewed, shopping interactions, approximate location, device and browser details, referral source and timestamps, and Clarity may use cookies to link activity into multi-page sessions. If you allow marketing, Meta, TikTok and Pinterest may process page, product, bag and checkout interactions together with campaign, device and browser identifiers. If you join Court Notes, we process the email address you submit, your subscription status and the delivery and engagement records needed to operate the list. The hosting provider also processes routine request information to deliver and protect the site.</p></section>
      <section><h2>3. Checkout and orders</h2><p>When you proceed to checkout, the product variants and quantities in your bag are used to create a Fourthwall cart. Campaign parameters, pseudonymous analytics identifiers and your site privacy choice may be passed with that cart so the storefront and resulting order can be measured consistently. Racquet Habit does not collect payment-card details on this site. Fourthwall processes order, contact, delivery, payment, tax and support information as merchant and fulfillment partner.</p></section>
      <section><h2>4. Court Notes</h2><p>Brevo processes Court Notes subscriptions and email delivery for Racquet Habit. We use double opt-in: submitting the form asks Brevo to send a confirmation message, and the address is added to the active list only after its confirmation link is used. Brevo may process the submitted address, subscription and unsubscribe timestamps, delivery status, bounces, and message-open or link-click activity where permitted by your email client and applicable law. Court Notes is separate from the website cookie choice because you request it directly by submitting the form. Every marketing message includes an unsubscribe link.</p></section>
      <section><h2>5. Cookies, analytics and advertising</h2><p>Microsoft Clarity and the Google tag load on every visit using consent-aware measurement. In the United States, first-party Google Analytics storage may be enabled by default on an opt-out basis while Google advertising storage and personalization remain denied. In other regions, Google Analytics starts without analytics storage and sends limited cookieless measurement pings unless you allow analytics. A saved choice or a Global Privacy Control signal overrides the regional default. Before analytics consent, Clarity receives cookieless, page-level interaction data but does not set Clarity cookies or link activity into a persistent multi-page session. Allowing analytics enables cookie-backed Google Analytics and multi-page Clarity continuity. Clarity advertising storage remains denied because Racquet Habit does not use Microsoft Ads. Marketing consent separately enables the Meta Pixel, TikTok Pixel and Pinterest tag for campaign measurement, attribution and audience features. Fourthwall has its own privacy choices on the hosted storefront and checkout. Where supported, Fourthwall sends checkout and paid-order events to connected advertising platforms; Pinterest paid-order measurement is sent through a signed server webhook only when the Racquet Habit cart records marketing consent. Pinterest may receive a one-way SHA-256 hash of the checkout email for event matching; the plain email is not sent by Racquet Habit to Pinterest.</p></section>
      <section><h2>6. Sharing and retention</h2><p>Depending on your choices and actions, information is processed by Cloudflare, Brevo, Fourthwall, Microsoft, Google, Meta, TikTok and Pinterest under their respective service and privacy terms. Clarity playback data is generally retained for 30 days; sessions marked as favorites may be retained for up to nine months. Hosting security logs may be retained by the hosting provider under its operational policies, order information is retained by Fourthwall according to its legal and service requirements, and newsletter records are retained while you remain subscribed or as needed to honor an unsubscribe and meet legal obligations. Each measurement provider controls retention for information it receives; Racquet Habit does not use advertising-event data to make decisions about eligibility, credit, employment, health or other sensitive matters.</p></section>
      <section><h2>7. Your choices</h2><p>Choose “No optional cookies,” or use “Cookie settings” in the footer at any time to change analytics and marketing choices. When analytics storage is denied, Google Analytics and Clarity continue only with limited cookieless measurement; they do not set analytics cookies or retain a persistent analytics identity from this site. Revoking analytics asks Clarity to remove its cookies and changes future Google events to cookieless measurement. Revoking marketing stops future marketing events from this site. Clearing site data removes the stored choice, bag and first-party identifiers accessible to this site. When the browser supplies a Global Privacy Control signal, this site keeps analytics storage and marketing tracking off. Browser privacy controls or content blockers may further limit measurement. Unsubscribe from Court Notes using the link in any message. For access, correction or deletion requests concerning an order, use Fourthwall order support. For questions about this site or Court Notes, contact Racquet Habit using the address on the contact page.</p></section>
      <section><h2>8. Changes</h2><p>Material changes will be posted here with a revised date. This notice will be updated when the measurement stack, checkout provider, email provider or handling of personal information materially changes.</p></section>
      <a class="paper-button" href="/contact">Privacy question <span>↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
